 "solana_notes": [
  "IDL ≈ Candid: generated from the program, consumed by M11 clients; freezing it lets M11 proceed in parallel, with the caveat that unreferenced account types are not yet in it",
  "event-cpi: the program invokes itself with the event bytes as instruction data signed by the __event_authority PDA, so events survive log truncation and are read from inner instructions (EVM logs can be truncated; ICP has no logs); it costs two extra accounts and roughly 2,100 CU per emit in LiteSVM",
  "InitSpace reserves the maximum size for Option/enum fields; Borsh writes a shorter prefix and the rest of the account stays zero; rent is paid on the reserved size"
 ]
